+# Symtropy Documentation Changelog — v3.0
+
+Date: 2026-07-21
+
+## Added
+
+- Protectorate federation, civil defense, and non-imperial authority contract;
+- twenty-thousand-unit institutional scale model;
+- unit registry, charter, recognition, capability, readiness, and interoperability runtime;
+- twenty local defense and resilience culture packets;
+- reserve mobilization, household cost, coalition command, communication delay, and demobilization runtime;
+- lawful refusal, unlawful abandonment, civilian oversight, strategic weapon control, and anti-warlord safeguards;
+- logistics, rescue, medical transfer, evacuation, evidence, surrender, missing-person, and recovery runtime;
+- multirole Protectorate ship and regional response formation atlas;
+- v3.0 benchmark schema, reference fixture, and one-hundred-ticket backlog;
+- v2.6 canon registry, v2.3 dependency map, roadmap, and readiness matrix.
+
+## Corrected Direction
+
+The Protectorate is not canonically one army and its tens of thousands of organizations are not all militias. Armed defense is one function within a larger protection ecology grounded in local charters, professional services, logistics, civilian oversight, and temporary coalition command.
+
+## Evidence
+
+All v3.0 systems remain D3 / I0. Strategic scale and performance envelopes remain D2 / I0 until executable profiling exists.
