+# Canon Registry and Document Governance
+
+## Purpose
+
+Integrate the v3.0 Protectorate federation without turning mutual defense into one imperial military faction, making every unit a militia, or allowing player command to erase local legitimacy and civilian authority.
+
+# v3.0 Ownership
+
+[Protectorate Federation, Civil Defense, and Non-Imperial Authority Contract](./PROTECTORATE_FEDERATION_CIVIL_DEFENSE_AND_NON_IMPERIAL_AUTHORITY_CONTRACT_V0_1.md) owns the federation's purpose, membership layers, protection domains, local legitimacy, bounded force, and non-imperial limits.
+
+[Protectorate Refusal Rights, Civilian Oversight, and Anti-Warlord Safeguards Contract](./PROTECTORATE_REFUSAL_RIGHTS_CIVILIAN_OVERSIGHT_AND_ANTI_WARLORD_SAFEGUARDS_CONTRACT_V0_1.md) owns lawful refusal, unlawful abandonment, strategic weapon control, emergency authority, detention safeguards, anti-capture architecture, and institutional repair.
+
+[Protectorate Unit Registry, Charter, Interoperability, and Local Legitimacy Runtime](../tech/PROTECTORATE_UNIT_REGISTRY_CHARTER_INTEROPERABILITY_AND_LOCAL_LEGITIMACY_RUNTIME_V0_1.md) owns persistent unit identity, charter provenance, recognition graphs, readiness, capability evidence, and interoperability.
+
+[Reserve Mobilization, Coalition Command, and Mission Scoping Runtime](../tech/RESERVE_MOBILIZATION_COALITION_COMMAND_AND_MISSION_SCOPING_RUNTIME_V0_1.md) owns alerts, reserve call-up, household cost, temporary coalitions, authority graphs, communications partitions, scope amendments, demobilization, and review.
+
+[Protectorate Logistics, Rescue, Medical, Evidence, and Recovery Runtime](../tech/PROTECTORATE_LOGISTICS_RESCUE_MEDICAL_EVIDENCE_AND_RECOVERY_RUNTIME_V0_1.md) owns material flow, triage, evacuation, protected corridors, repair, missing persons, source-chain recovery, evidence, surrender, and post-crisis restoration.
+
+[Protectorate Militia Cultures, Professions, and Local Defense Atlas](../lore/PROTECTORATE_MILITIA_CULTURES_PROFESSIONS_AND_LOCAL_DEFENSE_ATLAS_V0_1.md) owns local unit cultures, professions, visual identity, recruitment, ordinary life, and generational change.
+
+[Protectorate Ship, Fleet, and Regional Response Formation Atlas](../lore/PROTECTORATE_SHIP_FLEET_AND_REGIONAL_RESPONSE_FORMATION_ATLAS_V0_1.md) owns multirole Protectorate vessel families, small-craft ecology, formation doctrine, protected convoy play, and peace-time service.
+
+[Protectorate Twenty-Thousand-Unit Federation Benchmark](../ops/PROTECTORATE_20000_UNIT_FEDERATION_BENCHMARK_V0_1.md) owns promotion evidence.
+
+# v3.0 Canonical Decisions
+
+- The Protectorate is a federation of protection institutions, not one army.
+- Militia is one unit family among rescue, medical, infrastructure, ecological, logistics, evidence, strategic, and training organizations.
+- Local units retain charter provenance, culture, constituency relationships, and refusal rights.
+- Shared standards preserve interoperability without requiring cultural uniformity.
+- Capability claims, certification, observed performance, and current readiness are separate states.
+- Coalition command is temporary, mission-scoped, graph-structured, and reviewable.
+- Emergency authority expires unless lawfully renewed.
+- Strategic force requires distributed authorization.
+- Logistics, rescue, care, evidence, demobilization, and recovery are first-class protection gameplay.
+- Protectorate carriers remain multirole civic ships whose legitimacy does not follow from weapons or size.
+- The player can participate, lead, reform, refuse, and command without owning people or the federation.
+- The Protectorate may fail through capture, inequality, abandonment, secrecy, or permanent emergency rule.
+
