+# Symtropy Game Implementation Roadmap
+
+## Strategy
+
+The Protectorate is a long-horizon federation, but its first proof must be intimate: one local unit, known residents, real equipment, one difficult mobilization, and consequences after the alarm ends.
+
+# Gate A — Preserve the Playable Civilian Spine
+
+Complete Firstlight, the Continuance Crawler, professions, persistent households, and local infrastructure.
+
+**Exit:** there are real people and systems for a protection institution to serve.
+
+# Gate B — One Chartered Unit
+
+Implement persistent identity, charter, five capabilities, equipment, readiness, recognition, and ten named members.
+
+**Exit:** the unit can explain who authorized it and what it can actually do.
+
+# Gate C — One Local Incident
+
+Implement contested warning, partial call-up, household cost, transport, rescue, and demobilization.
+
+**Exit:** mobilization draws from real civilian life and returns to it.
+
+# Gate D — Two-Unit Interoperability
+
+Add a culturally different partner unit, adapter needs, shared medical transfer, and one command mismatch.
+
+**Exit:** cooperation works without making units identical.
+
+# Gate E — Scoped Coalition Command
+
+Implement one temporary coalition, delegated medical and engineering authority, delayed orders, and one mission amendment.
+
+**Exit:** command is useful, bounded, and source-chain visible.
+
+# Gate F — Refusal and Oversight
+
+Implement lawful professional refusal, malicious abandonment, anti-retaliation, civilian review, and institutional repair.
+
+**Exit:** refusal cannot be reduced to a morality prompt.
+
+# Gate G — Protectorate Convoy
+
+Implement one mixed civilian convoy with rescue reserve, surrender, damage, logistics, and recovery.
+
+**Exit:** success is measured by preserved continuity, not kill count.
+
+# Gate H — Multirole Response Carrier
+
+Implement a bounded Bastionline prototype with harbor, clinic, fabrication, habitation, rescue craft, and distributed command.
+
+**Exit:** the vessel remains a civic institution during peace and crisis.
+
+# Gate I — Strategic Federation Kernel
+
+Scale unit registry and mobilization to 500 operational units while preserving named people and local legitimacy.
+
+**Exit:** strategic compression is deterministic and legible.
+
+# Gate J — Twenty-Thousand-Unit Benchmark
+
+Run Meridian Fracture, performance telemetry, multiplayer authority tests, ablations, accessibility review, and delayed recall.
+
+**Exit:** representative gates pass and limitations are published.
+
+# Deferred
+
+- production-scale galactic Protectorate;
+- hundreds of fully simulated carriers;
+- open-ended strategic warfare;
+- autonomous weapon policy across every alien ontology;
+- complete planetary evacuation simulation;
+- long-horizon institutional evolution over centuries;
+- player-founded federation spanning multiple star systems.
+
+# Kill Rules
+
+- Cut unit count before cutting local identity.
+- Cut tactical detail before teleporting logistics.
+- Cut command breadth before granting absolute authority.
+- Cut weapon variety before cutting rescue and recovery.
+- Cut carrier count before making one carrier morally infallible.
+- Do not let Protectorate work replace ordinary settlement, profession, and relationship gameplay.
+
+## Roadmap Maxim
+
+> **First prove that one local unit can protect people without standing above them. Then scale the federation without losing the local truth that made protection legitimate.**
