+# v3.0 Protectorate Federation, Civil Defense, and Coalition Command Campaign
+
+## Campaign Question
+
+Can Symtropy support tens of thousands of locally rooted defense and resilience organizations while keeping protection culturally plural, materially constrained, lawfully bounded, and playable from volunteer scale to system-scale command?
+
+## Answer
+
+The Protectorate is now specified as a federation of protection institutions rather than one universal army.
+
+Its member ecology includes rescue, medicine, infrastructure, logistics, ecological response, communications, evidence, local armed defense, strategic fleets, training, and nonhuman partner formations.
+
+## Ten-Patch Spine
+
+1. federation and non-imperial authority contract;
+2. unit registry, charter, recognition, capability and readiness runtime;
+3. militia cultures, professions and local defense atlas;
+4. reserve mobilization, coalition command and mission scope runtime;
+5. refusal rights, civilian oversight and anti-warlord safeguards;
+6. logistics, rescue, medical, evidence and recovery runtime;
+7. Protectorate ship, fleet and regional formation atlas;
+8. twenty-thousand-unit benchmark, schema and reference fixture;
+9. one-hundred-ticket implementation backlog;
+10. canon, dependency, roadmap, readiness, manifest, audit and reconstruction integration.
+
+## Major Decisions
+
+- Tens of thousands of units are plausible across planets, carriers, habitats, convoys, oceans, machines, and alien partners.
+- Only a minority need be combat-focused.
+- Local legitimacy and strategic interoperability coexist.
+- Mobilization draws from households and institutions rather than creating free personnel.
+- Coalition authority is temporary and distributed by function.
+- Refusal is protected but not consequence-free.
+- Civilian oversight can fail and remains a simulated institution.
+- Protectorate carriers are multirole rescue, repair, shelter, logistics, and defense civilizations.
+- Recovery, evidence, demobilization, and institutional repair remain part of every serious crisis.
+
+## Production Boundary
+
+The campaign does not claim that the systems are implemented. All remain D3 / I0, with strategic performance targets at D2 / I0.
+
+The first playable proof should be one local unit attached to a known settlement and Continuance route—not an immediate galaxy-wide strategy layer.
+
+## Campaign Maxim
+
+> **Scale the promise of mutual protection only as quickly as the simulation can preserve the people, charters, supplies, refusals, and consequences that make the promise trustworthy.**
